 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Variant 3 (inferred follow-up): board is a non-empty rectangular list of integer rows (N rows, M columns) and 0 <= p < M. A path starts at (0, p), every move stays inside the grid, and the path ends as soon as it enters row N - 1 (when N = 1 the path is just the start cell). The score of a path is the sum of the board values of the cells it visits, including the start and the final cell. From (i, j) a move goes to (i + 1, j - 1), (i + 1, j), (i + 1, j + 1) or, as a special jump, to (i + 2, j); the jumped-over cell (i + 1, j) is not visited. At most k special jumps are used on one path (k >= 0). Return one maximum-score path as the list of its visited cells [row, column], from the start to the bottom-row cell; among maximum-score paths return the lexicographically smallest list (cells compared by row, then column).",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
